    "result_text": "The full suite is green (16 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `riskFlag` for owners following the codebase's established **derived-getter** pattern (the same shape used by `getContactPreference`, `getOwnerSegment`, etc.), so it required no pipeline or mapper changes \u2014 MapStruct auto-maps the new property and the existing `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline surfaces it.\n\nThree changes, each in the place its logic belongs:\n\n1. **`util/DisposableEmailDomains.java`** \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent(String email)`, a genuinely distinct check from the existing exact `isBlocked`. This matters: exact disposable domains are *rejected at creation*, so `isBlocked` can never fire on a persisted owner. \"Disposable-adjacent\" matches domains sharing a blocked domain's registrable base label \u2014 catching subdomains (`signup.mailinator.com`) and look-alikes on other TLDs (`mailinator.net`), which pass creation but still smell disposable. I refactored the shared \"domain after last `@`\" logic into a private `domainOf` helper so both checks reuse it (behavior of `isBlocked` unchanged).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getRiskFlag()`, an OR of the three specified signals, each mapped to an existing concept: `isPossibleDuplicate()` (possible duplicate), `DisposableEmailDomains.isDisposableAdjacent(email)` (disposable-adjacent email), and `isCapacityWarning()` (city over its soft capacity \u2014 the persisted flag captured when the city held \u226540 owners).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema alongside the other derived flags, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\nThe target test `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` and all 16 tests pass.",
